{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/58052-strike-first-embed-vs-celerity-discipline","id":58052,"title":"Strike First Embed vs Celerity Discipline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-26T06:22:07-08:00","id":58052,"title":"Strike First Embed vs Celerity Discipline","content":"Hey guys, the title says it all really. If a Demon is facing off against a Vampire and activates the Strike First embed to act first in the combat then attacks the Vampire, the Vampire activates the Celerity Discipline to interrupt said attack. How would this resolve itself? The Strike First embed says that the Demon can use the embed even if he's surprised, so it kinda comes across like Strike First ignores initiative for the Demons first action. If the vampire interrupts the attack with any instant action, then the demon isn't acting first in the combat, so kinda renders the effects of the reflexive embed null and void. If anyone could clarify this riddle for me, that would be greatly appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some day we'll look back on this, laugh awkwardly and change the subject.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1889-thefrigidmidget","name":"TheFrigidMidget","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T06:27:41-08:00","id":58054,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a great situation for the Clash of Wills rule to me. The powers are mutually contradictory; enter roll-off to see which one trumps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T06:30:56-08:00","id":58057,"title":"","content":"Face palm. How did I not think of that? Cheers man, much appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some day we'll look back on this, laugh awkwardly and change the subject.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1889-thefrigidmidget","name":"TheFrigidMidget","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T07:01:43-08:00","id":58070,"title":"","content":"Alternatively the interrupt ability of Celerity triumphs as that doesn't make the Vampire 'go first' it makes them act 'during'.<br /> <br /> So the Demon still acts first, begins the strike and then the Vampire interrupts. Kind of up to you how you want to treat that. Because in the scenario of someone going faster than the Vampire they can interrupt it normally anyway. I'd personally rule this way because Strike First essentially moves you to the top of the initiative order and buffs the initiative roll while Celerity trumps the initiative order with the interrupt.<br /> <br /> Now if both Demon and Vampire tried to use their powers to be at the top of initiative then I'd roll Clash of Wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T09:07:02-08:00","id":58117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/58052-strike-first-embed-vs-celerity-discipline?p=58054#post58054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a great situation for the Clash of Wills rule to me. The powers are mutually contradictory; enter roll-off to see which one trumps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded. This is exactly the kind of &quot;But MY power says ... &quot; issue Clash of Wills addresses (&quot;My power says I'm hidden.&quot; &quot;But MY power reveals the hidden!&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T09:21:10-08:00","id":58125,"title":"","content":"Yeah, looking at both the Demon PDF, and the B&amp;S PDF, I'd say it's pretty clear that this situation would be a Clash of Wills, with Vamp rolling Blood Potency + Celerity vs the Demon rolling Wits + Primum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}